# What this establishes, stated precisely:
#  - /dev/kvm exists, is group `kvm`, and goes crw-rw---- -> crw-rw-rw- after
#    the exact udev rule GitHub's 2024-04-02 changelog documents, reload,
#    trigger, settle. The udev-rule mechanism works on this runner image.
#  - The CPU reports `svm` (AMD-V) — this runner's underlying hardware does
#    expose virtualization extensions.
#  - The guest was NEVER booted. `qemu-system-x86_64` was never invoked.
#    The failure is entirely at kernel *acquisition*: the attempt-1 script
#    (which this excerpt shows running) tried the runner's own currently
#    running kernel at exactly this path, which is present but 0600
#    root:root — unreadable by the plain runner user before any
#    privileged copy step. That is the exact bug this commit's rewritten
#    spikes/s9/scripts/kvm-boot-check.sh (sudo cp + chown to an owned,
#    0644 copy) targets — a fix validated under the same non-root
#    boundary locally (results/kernel-acquisition-nonroot.log), but this
